<item><title>Western Cape water allocations cut as dam storage drops</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ls/western-cape-water-allocations-cut-as-dam-storage-drops-438b1d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ls/western-cape-water-allocations-cut-as-dam-storage-drops-438b1d/</guid><category>Lesotho</category><description>Water and Sanitation Minister Pemmy Majodina announced a 7% cut for domestic and industrial users and 15% for irrigation.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:29:59 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ls/western-cape-water-allocations-cut-as-dam-storage-drops-438b1d/share.jpg" length="39476" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ls/western-cape-water-allocations-cut-as-dam-storage-drops-438b1d/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
